# The bird doesn't gain an attack; it is replaced. The client keeps this skill's
# animations under a `summon` node, and the 6th job skill that uses it says
# "while Fury of the Wild is summoned", so for forty seconds the Phoenix or
# Frostprey is this.
#
# 3.42 seconds isn't published anywhere. It is twice the 1.71 used for the two
# birds, which matches their animations: theirs run 1170ms and this one
# 2310ms, almost exactly double. `attackAfter` is not the period: both birds
# state 450 against a real 1710.
#
# Reach is GMS's 10: the summon's attack box is 730x240, and floor(730/70) is
# exactly 10.
#
# Damage is GMS's 450 + 15x on seven lines: 465% at level 1 and 900% at 30. A
# pulse on its own clock gets no Final Attack and no Shadow Partner, like every
# summon here: nothing the character didn't swing is doubled.
#
# Every explorer archer has a bird by their 3rd job, so GMS's "only while one is
# summoned" needs no gate.
name: "Fury of the Wild"
description:
  "Fills your summoned bird with an older, wilder power, and for a while it "
  "hunts as the thing it used to be."
kind: SKILL_KIND_ACTIVE
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_BOW_MASTER_V skill_order: 11 }
placement { job_advancement: JOB_ADVANCEMENT_MARKSMAN_V skill_order: 5 }
v_node: V_NODE_KIND_ARCHETYPE
max_level: 30
base_delay_ms: 120
cooldown_seconds: 119.5
cooldown_seconds_per_level: -0.5
buff {
  duration_seconds: 40.0
  pulse {
    label: "Empowered Summon"
    cast_interval_seconds: 3.42
    max_enemies: 10
    lines: 7
    base { skill_pct: 4.65 }
    per_level { skill_pct: 0.15 }
  }
}
